{"id":"CVE-2006-1966","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-04-21T10:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T17:35:30.616Z","description":"An unspecified Fortinet product, possibly Fortinet28, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service via a \"small synflood\" to the SMTP port (TCP port 25), as demonstrated by a 10-microsecond wait between sending packets.  NOTE: this issue has been disputed in followup posts that suggest that a protection feature is triggering a RST.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/431404/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060416 Fortinet28 box does not resist has small synflood!"},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/fulldisclosure/2006-04/0449.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20060418 Re: Fortinet28 box does not resist has small synflood!"},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/fulldisclosure/2006-04/0472.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20060418 Re: Fortinet28 box does not resist has small synflood!"}],"vendors":["fortinet"]}
